course: dictionary
lesson: 13982
title: Who is a lodger?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lodger is a person who pays money to live in a room in someone else's house. Lodgers often share the kitchen and bathroom with the family, but they are not part of the family. «The Patels took in a lodger to help pay for the house.» The words «took in» and «pay» tell you the lodger is a paying guest who lives there.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Our lodger has her own room and shares the kitchen with us.» Her own room, shared kitchen and the word «us» show she lives in the house but is not one of the family. Ask yourself: does this person pay to live here? If yes, they are probably a lodger.
explain: A guest visits for a short time and usually does not pay. A lodger lives in the house for a longer time and pays rent. «The lodger paid rent every Friday.» Rent is the money you pay to live somewhere, so the word «rent» is a clue that the lodger is paying to stay.
fact: A lodger is a person who pays to live in a room in someone else's house.
fact: A lodger often shares the kitchen and bathroom with the family.
fact: «Take in a lodger» means to let a stranger pay to live in your house.
fact: «Rent» is the money a lodger pays to stay, often every week or every month.
fact: Rare meaning: a lodger can also be anyone staying for a time in a place.
exercise: «The Patels took in a lodger to help pay for the house.» What is a lodger? | *A person who pays to live in a room in someone else's house | A person who builds houses | A person who owns the house and the land | A person who cleans the house every day
exercise: Ella says, «The lodger is part of the family.» Is she right? | Yes, every lodger is a cousin | *No, a lodger pays to live in the house but is not family | No, because lodgers never live in houses | Yes, because lodgers always share the same surname
exercise: Find and copy the word from the sentence «Our lodger has her own room and shares the kitchen with us.» that means a person who lives in the house and pays for it. | *lodger | kitchen | room | shares
test: Lodgers often share which rooms with the family? | The attic and the garage | The shop and the school | The bedroom and the garden | *The kitchen and bathroom
test: What does «take in a lodger» mean? | *To let a person pay to live in your house | To hire a new cook for the kitchen | To adopt a child from another family | To send a letter to a stranger
exam: In «The lodger paid rent every Friday», what does rent mean? | *Money paid to live in a place | A type of food | A key to the front door | A way of cleaning the house
